---
args:
  inventory: '{ id: string; author: string; domain: string; operation: string; sizableFixture: boolean; referenceOk: boolean; sourceReviewState: string; collected: boolean }[]'
  priorityOrder: 'string[]'
returns: '{ selected: string[]; pending: string[]; reasons: string[] }'
---
Select the next semantic-stack generation snapshot.

1. Read inventory and priorityOrder. Prefer the owner's substantive semantic programs before ordinary refill work.
2. Keep held or incomplete sources pending. A source needs a coherent sizable fixture, independently derived semantic oracle, exact source/reference evidence, and an explicit generation preparation state. Preparation does not grant training admission.
3. Among prepared uncollected sources, follow the supplied authored order, which interleaves domains and distinct operations. Preserve the whole-program and whole-world identities.
4. If real nested-call and scoped-capture behavior remains unmeasured for a new interface, select a clearly identified diagnostic subset before treating the full program as teacher collection input. Its results remain diagnostic evidence until reviewed.
5. Return selected IDs, pending IDs, and a precise reason for each pending item. Keep incomplete broad-catalog designs visible for the next fixture-authoring pass.
